WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.620 --> 00:03.860
What would you say if I told you I’m…

3
00:04.440 --> 00:06.340
not interested in the opposite sex?

4
00:06.860 --> 00:08.100
It’s Ruth, right?

5
00:11.000 --> 00:12.000
Ji.

6
00:12.920 --> 00:14.470
Ji, is that you?

7
00:14.920 --> 00:18.110
Wow, you’re all grown up now.

8
00:18.650 --> 00:21.080
Is this Ms. Ornrampha?

9
00:22.090 --> 00:23.330
How do you know her, Ji?

10
02:04.930 --> 02:08.140
MR. JIRA, MS. NARUMON, MS. ORNRAMPHA JITRADA, JIRAPHAT, THEERARUTH, IRIN

11
02:08.180 --> 02:10.140
Why does it say ‘Theeraruth’?

12
02:10.470 --> 02:12.220
Isn’t his name Atiwitch?

13
02:12.600 --> 02:15.550
You knew Ruth before, Ji?

14
02:15.770 --> 02:17.640
How come you never told me that?

15
02:18.710 --> 02:20.310
How could someone like Ji remember that?

16
02:20.670 --> 02:24.360
He doesn’t even remember what he ate yesterday.

17
02:25.330 --> 02:26.670
But don’t forget, Jean.

18
02:26.960 --> 02:28.590
After what happened,

19
02:28.620 --> 02:31.620
we agreed that if Ji couldn’t remember anything,

20
02:31.660 --> 02:32.750
we would let it go

21
02:33.080 --> 02:34.420
and never mention it again.

22
02:36.260 --> 02:38.700
Ma’am, I think I smell something burning.

23
02:40.580 --> 02:42.310
Oh, no! I left the fish in the pan!

24
02:46.410 --> 02:49.160
Enough about me. Do you even remember what happened?

25
02:49.190 --> 02:50.620
I’m not like you.

26
02:51.210 --> 02:55.870
Besides, do you know that even though Mom and Ms. Orn don’t see each other,

27
02:55.890 --> 02:57.090
they always talk on the phone?

28
02:57.840 --> 02:59.400
Why has nobody ever told me about this?

29
02:59.770 --> 03:01.800
It was a long time ago.

30
03:02.550 --> 03:04.440
You were in Grade 1.

31
03:04.860 --> 03:06.300
What’s the point of telling you?

32
03:07.330 --> 03:10.940
How did our family and their family know each other then?

33
03:11.450 --> 03:12.450
It’s a long story.

34
03:18.960 --> 03:20.810
You can unload these things from the truck.

35
03:20.840 --> 03:22.420
- Yes, ma’am. - Please be careful.

36
03:22.740 --> 03:23.740
- Mom. - Hmm?

37
03:23.880 --> 03:24.930
Where’s Papa?

38
03:25.160 --> 03:27.120
Papa and Khun have work to do.

39
03:27.590 --> 03:29.750
The three of us have to stay here by ourselves for now.

40
03:30.130 --> 03:31.820
Do you want to see Papa, Ruth?

41
03:31.860 --> 03:32.960
I can take you to see him.

42
03:35.830 --> 03:37.620
(Don’t run, Ji. You’ll fall.)

43
03:37.650 --> 03:38.960
I won’t, Mom.

44
03:46.550 --> 03:47.550
Who’s that?

45
03:50.590 --> 03:51.180
Luke?

46
03:51.540 --> 03:52.540
Ruth.

47
03:52.600 --> 03:53.600
Ruke?

48
03:54.160 --> 03:54.710
Ruth.

49
03:54.940 --> 03:56.170
Ugh, I don’t like it.

50
03:56.480 --> 03:57.440
It’s hard to pronounce.

51
03:57.460 --> 04:00.080
Ruth’s first name is Theeraruth.

52
04:00.380 --> 04:02.080
You can call him Tee instead.

53
04:02.490 --> 04:04.060
Okay, that’s better.

54
04:04.550 --> 04:05.560
What’s up, Tee?

55
04:12.510 --> 04:13.510
Ji.

56
04:13.980 --> 04:15.166
You can’t leave the school grounds.

57
04:15.190 --> 04:16.870
We have ten minutes before the van leaves.

58
04:16.900 --> 04:17.900
Let’s go grab a bite.

59
04:20.520 --> 04:22.650
(My mama says candy is bad.)

60
04:22.680 --> 04:23.680
(It causes cavities.)

61
04:23.900 --> 04:24.986
This is fishing monkey candy.

62
04:25.010 --> 04:26.720
My mom says eating fish makes you smart.

63
04:34.000 --> 04:36.000
Keep trying. You’ll get the hang of it.

64
04:36.020 --> 04:37.200
- (Honey.) - Yeah?

65
04:37.230 --> 04:38.800
(Can you bring out another table?)

66
04:40.320 --> 04:41.320
That’s enough.

67
04:41.700 --> 04:42.940
It’s okay if you can’t ride it.

68
04:43.400 --> 04:44.400
Don’t worry.

69
04:45.460 --> 04:46.460
(Today...)

70
04:47.530 --> 04:49.610
(I’ll take you for a ride around the block.)

71
04:50.550 --> 04:52.180
(Because you’ve been a good boy.)

72
04:54.020 --> 04:55.020
(You’re the best)

73
04:59.820 --> 05:03.060
(Honey, have you got everything? (I’m almost ready.)

74
05:03.230 --> 05:06.040
(Hey, I’m ready. Here.)

75
05:06.060 --> 05:07.750
We’re going to the beach, kids.

76
05:08.090 --> 05:09.520
Yay!

77
05:09.560 --> 05:11.660
Okay, let’s go. We’re all set.

78
05:43.230 --> 05:45.960
Ji, let’s go home. This place is creepy.

79
05:46.280 --> 05:47.520
Not at all.

80
06:07.980 --> 06:09.390
Tee, wake up!

81
06:15.380 --> 06:17.010
Use this. Don’t drop it.

82
06:17.720 --> 06:19.370
Hold my hand. Don’t ever let go.

83
06:19.990 --> 06:20.990
1...

84
06:21.540 --> 06:22.540
2...

85
06:23.060 --> 06:24.060
3.

86
06:24.460 --> 06:25.100
Please!

87
06:25.320 --> 06:26.320
Keep off!

88
06:30.270 --> 06:31.290
Ruth! Ruth!

89
06:31.980 --> 06:32.980
Excuse me.

90
06:33.490 --> 06:34.370
- Ruth! Ruth! - Ji!

91
06:34.400 --> 06:35.400
Mom!

92
06:40.910 --> 06:42.720
- (Are you okay?) - (Ji!)

93
06:43.100 --> 06:44.100
Ji!

94
06:44.140 --> 06:44.650
Ji

95
06:44.900 --> 06:45.710
Ji. Baby!

96
06:45.730 --> 06:46.730
- Ji! - Ji!

97
06:47.600 --> 06:48.600
- Are you alright? - Ji!

98
07:16.110 --> 07:16.480
Ruth!

99
07:16.510 --> 07:17.980
Ruth! Ruth! Ruth! Ruth!

100
07:18.020 --> 07:20.010
Sir! Sir! We need help here!

101
07:20.180 --> 07:21.680
Ruth! Ruth! Baby!

102
07:21.710 --> 07:22.840
Ruth! Ruth!

103
07:23.560 --> 07:24.560
Please help!

104
07:34.420 --> 07:35.420
Ruth’s awake.

105
07:36.360 --> 07:38.220
Ruth, how are you?

106
07:40.610 --> 07:42.220
Easy, easy. You’re safe now.

107
07:48.420 --> 07:49.420
Mom...

108
07:49.830 --> 07:50.510
Where’s Ji?

109
07:50.820 --> 07:53.060
Why would you want to see the one who put you in danger?

110
07:54.200 --> 07:55.200
Honey.

111
07:57.620 --> 07:59.340
Ji is okay now.

112
07:59.660 --> 08:01.340
But he needs to rest, okay?

113
08:01.360 --> 08:02.550
We’ll visit him later.

114
08:03.820 --> 08:06.520
Ruth, after you’re released from the hospital,

115
08:06.910 --> 08:08.310
let’s move back to our house, okay?

116
08:10.310 --> 08:12.870
You’ll get to go to the same school as Tawan,

117
08:12.890 --> 08:13.980
Pim, and Lita again.

118
08:14.460 --> 08:15.460
Are you glad, honey?

119
08:18.280 --> 08:22.640
But… if you don’t want to move back, you don’t have to.

120
08:22.660 --> 08:23.780
Whatever you want.

121
08:24.310 --> 08:25.760
What about Papa?

122
08:26.260 --> 08:29.470
Papa… will have to go back and forth

123
08:29.500 --> 08:31.470
because it’s far from where he works.

124
08:33.100 --> 08:34.470
I want to move back to our house.

125
08:34.500 --> 08:35.380
I’m glad, Mom.

126
08:35.420 --> 08:37.080
Mmm, okay.

127
08:41.260 --> 08:43.880
You can always come back here.

128
08:44.130 --> 08:45.620
Thank you so much, Mon.

129
08:45.980 --> 08:48.900
Both of you were always there for us.

130
08:49.300 --> 08:50.886
Lately, there have been nothing but bad rumors.

131
08:50.910 --> 08:53.590
I’m thinking of taking Ruth to change his name to ward off bad luck.

132
08:53.670 --> 08:54.540
Good luck.

133
08:54.560 --> 08:56.540
I’ll miss you guys.

134
08:57.990 --> 09:01.440
(From that day on, I completely forgot about everything.)

135
09:02.420 --> 09:04.420
(The memories of Theeraruth)

136
09:05.050 --> 09:08.260
(were buried beneath a pile of forgotten old CDs.)

137
09:08.280 --> 09:10.090
That’s what happened.

138
09:12.090 --> 09:13.200
Did I forget anything?

139
09:14.230 --> 09:15.500
That’s pretty much it.

140
09:16.120 --> 09:17.320
After that incident,

141
09:17.600 --> 09:20.320
their family transferred their son back to his former private school.

142
09:20.770 --> 09:24.580
I’m surprised Ruth and Ji have become close again.

143
09:26.190 --> 09:27.190
Hey.

144
09:27.690 --> 09:29.320
Hey, Kong. Hey, Kong.

145
09:31.170 --> 09:32.170
Wake up.

146
09:32.220 --> 09:33.300
They’ve finished the story.

147
09:33.900 --> 09:37.890
Ty's Songkran ordeal was more entertaining.

148
09:38.760 --> 09:41.500
Sorry my life is so uneventful.

149
09:42.830 --> 09:45.740
It might sound trivial now,

150
09:46.120 --> 09:48.420
but I was really shocked back then.

151
09:48.450 --> 09:51.910
I was so shocked I didn't know what to do.

152
09:52.910 --> 09:55.060
It’s good you didn’t remember it back then.

153
09:57.140 --> 09:58.740
Mom, let me help.

154
09:59.260 --> 10:00.440
I’ll help, too.

155
10:07.250 --> 10:08.250
Ji.

156
10:08.560 --> 10:10.620
Honestly, the story of you and your friend Ruth

157
10:10.660 --> 10:12.460
is more entertaining than the dramas I watch.

158
10:12.820 --> 10:13.900
What are you talking about?

159
10:14.640 --> 10:15.750
Think about it.

160
10:16.460 --> 10:17.870
You two grew up together.

161
10:18.310 --> 10:19.880
Your parents are close.

162
10:19.920 --> 10:21.540
You used to be neighbors.

163
10:21.720 --> 10:23.706
You’ve escaped a life-and-death situation together.

164
10:23.730 --> 10:25.640
And you get to see each other again.

165
10:27.430 --> 10:29.210
This is straight out of a romantic drama.

166
10:30.310 --> 10:31.310
It’s meant to be.

167
10:31.600 --> 10:32.800
It’s destiny.

168
10:34.950 --> 10:36.600
- Let’s go! - Tyler!

169
10:37.220 --> 10:39.090
(Kids, dinner’s ready.)

170
10:39.120 --> 10:40.690
Okay, we’re coming.

171
10:54.640 --> 10:56.980
Oh, have your friends left?

172
10:57.700 --> 10:58.700
Yes.

173
11:00.420 --> 11:01.520
Go take a shower, then?

174
11:01.540 --> 11:02.680
Why are you sitting here?

175
11:03.600 --> 11:06.180
Are you preparing the ingredients for tomorrow?

176
11:06.810 --> 11:08.910
Yes, but you don’t have to help me.

177
11:08.940 --> 11:10.330
I’m almost done.

178
11:10.350 --> 11:12.120
I’ll continue tomorrow.

179
11:14.220 --> 11:15.220
Well...

180
11:17.420 --> 11:19.020
If you don’t mind,

181
11:19.650 --> 11:22.000
can I ask you to do something tomorrow?

182
11:37.400 --> 11:40.520
(Maybe him looking at the sky that day)

183
11:40.780 --> 11:42.100
(was a sign of something.)

184
11:44.500 --> 11:45.880
(But I was too afraid to ask him.)

185
11:51.880 --> 11:52.420
Wow.

186
11:52.700 --> 11:55.030
Looks so tasty. Where did you buy it?

187
11:55.340 --> 11:56.360
My friend’s mom’s place.

188
11:56.980 --> 12:01.340
Oh. Have you guys decided which school you’re attending?

189
12:01.680 --> 12:02.680
Not yet.

190
12:02.770 --> 12:05.880
Then… why don’t we go to the same school?

191
12:06.150 --> 12:08.520
But there’s an entrance exam, right?

192
12:08.960 --> 12:09.960
Yeah.

193
12:10.760 --> 12:12.240
But don’t worry.

194
12:12.430 --> 12:14.940
It’s not a popular school.

195
12:14.980 --> 12:16.840
You don’t need to study that hard.

196
12:16.880 --> 12:21.520
Plus, there’s an egg yolk ice-cream shop nearby.

197
12:21.560 --> 12:23.500
Let’s go to this school, then.

198
12:24.890 --> 12:25.890
Wanna join us?

199
12:27.000 --> 12:28.000
Why not?

200
12:30.300 --> 12:31.300
(Eventually, )

201
12:31.720 --> 12:34.080
(I got a chance to be back in his world again.)

202
12:52.550 --> 12:54.600
How can you put up with that old mean teacher?

203
12:54.930 --> 12:56.290
He’s the only one

204
12:56.440 --> 12:59.900
who can convince Ms. Suda to meet us halfway.

205
13:00.460 --> 13:01.900
She just agreed to share her notes with us,

206
13:01.920 --> 13:02.926
but she’d probably still be so biased

207
13:02.950 --> 13:04.870
that students would end up skipping class again.

208
13:06.410 --> 13:08.060
There are some free seats over there.

209
13:08.100 --> 13:10.140
- Let’s ask him if we can have a seat. - Yeah.

210
13:10.490 --> 13:11.900
I think he’d rather be alone.

211
13:12.510 --> 13:14.040
Let’s sit somewhere else.

212
13:14.580 --> 13:16.160
Mmm, okay.

213
13:16.740 --> 13:18.500
Oh, he’s leaving.

214
13:18.540 --> 13:19.540
Come on.

215
13:27.850 --> 13:31.740
(If I had turned around and gotten to know him again that day, )

216
13:34.190 --> 13:35.716
(would things have turned out differently?)

217
13:35.740 --> 13:39.860
(would things have turned out differently?) JIRAPHAT JAROENWONG BORN: 31 OCTOBER 1993, DIED: 4 MARCH 2023

218
13:50.140 --> 13:53.000
STUDENT COUNCIL, NAWINA SCHOOL ATIWITCH RATTANAWATTHANA, CLASS PRESIDENT

219
13:54.020 --> 13:55.490
Oh, hi.

220
13:57.180 --> 13:58.180
Hi.

221
14:00.540 --> 14:02.360
Have you eaten?

222
14:02.710 --> 14:03.710
I have.

223
14:11.230 --> 14:12.230
Ruth.

224
14:13.790 --> 14:14.790
Hmm?

225
14:16.980 --> 14:18.380
I know the truth.

226
14:19.470 --> 14:20.470
The truth?

227
14:22.390 --> 14:23.390
Yes.

228
14:29.420 --> 14:30.420
You...

229
14:31.980 --> 14:33.430
You know everything?

230
14:34.040 --> 14:35.040
Yes.

231
14:35.720 --> 14:36.880
Everything.

232
14:38.040 --> 14:40.100
(Ji knows that I came back in time?)

233
14:41.750 --> 14:42.750
Does this mean…

234
14:44.360 --> 14:45.580
You know that…

235
14:46.750 --> 14:48.310
If I hadn’t figured it out myself,

236
14:49.200 --> 14:50.940
you wouldn’t have told me anyway?

237
14:52.790 --> 14:55.830
I thought you were living your best life.

238
14:56.700 --> 14:59.680
So I didn’t want to remind you of those sad memories.

239
15:00.080 --> 15:01.870
Wait a second. What sad memories?

240
15:01.900 --> 15:03.170
What’s sad about this?

241
15:06.670 --> 15:09.050
Here. Thai desserts by Ms. Narumon.

242
15:09.070 --> 15:10.740
A 100-year-old family recipe.

243
15:12.060 --> 15:15.440
But you have to come to my house to enjoy the hot cocoa.

244
15:16.230 --> 15:17.580
For today, just take these.

245
15:25.530 --> 15:28.410
This is ‘the truth’ you were talking about?

246
15:28.860 --> 15:31.880
That’s right, Theeraruth.

247
15:43.850 --> 15:44.850
You like them?

248
15:45.500 --> 15:46.500
Want some?

249
15:52.710 --> 15:53.710
Aren’t you mad?

250
15:55.140 --> 15:56.766
Even after my mom and Jean told me every detail,

251
15:56.790 --> 15:58.510
I couldn’t remember a thing.

252
15:58.970 --> 16:00.150
How can I be mad at you?

253
16:02.150 --> 16:03.890
I told you not to worry about it.

254
16:04.240 --> 16:06.230
You never came to me and said hi.

255
16:06.280 --> 16:07.790
And I forgot all about us.

256
16:07.820 --> 16:08.820
Let’s call it even.

257
16:13.340 --> 16:14.340
That’s fair, right?

258
16:15.440 --> 16:17.890
- Eat it up. You haven’t tried this. - Let’s share.

259
16:29.020 --> 16:33.430
THURSDAY, 16 SEPTEMBER 2010

260
16:36.870 --> 16:38.220
Should I let them know

261
16:38.250 --> 16:40.360
that they’re not alone in this room?

262
16:41.030 --> 16:42.030
Do you want to?

263
16:43.260 --> 16:44.260
Who would?

264
16:47.820 --> 16:51.640
These are the final exam guidelines. FRIDAY, 17 SEPTEMBER 2010

265
16:51.670 --> 16:53.796
Good luck with your exams, everyone. BHUJANGAPRAYATA CHANDA

266
16:53.820 --> 16:56.040
Attention, students.

267
16:56.330 --> 16:58.270
- Thank you, ma’am. - Thank you.

268
17:01.700 --> 17:03.920
The final exams are coming up before we know it.

269
17:04.110 --> 17:06.160
Besides, we have to prepare for Sports Day.

270
17:06.190 --> 17:07.040
Ugh.

271
17:07.080 --> 17:10.000
- Being in Grade 11 is so exhausting. - Facts.

272
17:10.360 --> 17:12.210
How are we supposed to find time to study?

273
17:12.640 --> 17:13.760
Why don’t we study together?

274
17:18.210 --> 17:20.210
Ruth said he’d tutor us.

275
17:20.800 --> 17:21.800
Ugh.

276
17:21.840 --> 17:22.840
Ruth again.

277
17:23.080 --> 17:24.730
All you talk about is Ruth.

278
17:25.840 --> 17:27.420
- Hey, are you blushing? - What?

279
17:27.460 --> 17:29.020
Gotcha.

280
17:29.050 --> 17:29.970
- Gotcha. - Hey, it’s not that.

281
17:30.000 --> 17:31.360
- Your ears are red. - They’re not.

282
17:46.060 --> 17:47.100
Why are you staring at me?

283
17:48.680 --> 17:49.680
Just want to look at you?

284
17:52.440 --> 17:53.720
I’ll charge you.

285
17:55.390 --> 17:56.400
I can pay.

286
18:03.130 --> 18:07.000
Now that my parents know we’re friends again,

287
18:08.000 --> 18:09.880
they want you to come over for dinner.

288
18:11.940 --> 18:13.160
Don’t worry.

289
18:13.400 --> 18:15.160
My mom and dad like you.

290
18:16.580 --> 18:17.890
- They do? - Yeah.

291
18:18.720 --> 18:19.720
Besides,

292
18:20.240 --> 18:21.630
I’ll be right there with you.

293
18:27.780 --> 18:29.340
- Okay then. - Really?

294
18:29.770 --> 18:31.690
Come over after the exam then.

295
18:31.920 --> 18:33.320
Kongpob and Tyler are coming, too.

296
18:33.600 --> 18:35.890
In case someone gets nervous.

297
18:43.220 --> 18:44.220
Finish your homework.

298
18:53.310 --> 18:55.070
Stop staring. Finish it.

299
18:59.880 --> 19:02.420
FINAL EXAM FRIDAY, 24 SEPTEMBER 2010

300
19:15.880 --> 19:17.880
School’s over!

301
19:18.020 --> 19:18.770
Wooo!

302
19:18.790 --> 19:19.460
Hey.

303
19:19.780 --> 19:22.130
You still have to come to Sports Day practice.

304
19:22.290 --> 19:25.230
If you don't show up, I'll charge you extra next semester.

305
19:25.410 --> 19:26.360
You wouldn't dare.

306
19:26.390 --> 19:27.580
Why wouldn't I?

307
19:27.660 --> 19:28.660
Okay, fine.

308
19:28.680 --> 19:30.370
- Scary. - Don’t play with me.

309
19:32.910 --> 19:34.370
- Yes, I’m done. - You’re done?

310
19:34.400 --> 19:35.720
Yeah, finally.

311
19:35.750 --> 19:37.520
(This semester went by so fast.)

312
19:37.940 --> 19:41.470
(Looking back, I've made so many wonderful memories)

313
19:41.510 --> 19:43.210
(with my friends in Class 7.)

314
19:44.600 --> 19:46.100
Move. Get out of my way.

315
19:46.130 --> 19:47.500
I’ll finish cleaning up so I can go home.

316
19:47.520 --> 19:48.820
Move it. Move it.

317
19:48.850 --> 19:50.450
Move it. Move it. Move it.

318
19:50.480 --> 19:52.360
Move it. I told you to move it.

319
19:52.380 --> 19:53.450
Out of my way.

320
19:54.170 --> 19:55.670
- What? - You think you’re the main character?

321
19:55.690 --> 19:57.260
Why are you standing here

322
19:57.300 --> 19:59.190
instead of helping me clean up so we can leave?

323
19:59.220 --> 20:00.420
- Whose duty is this? - Mine.

324
20:01.140 --> 20:02.910
Ji, Kong just called.

325
20:02.930 --> 20:04.490
He’s waiting for us in front of school.

326
20:04.520 --> 20:05.100
Hold on a sec.

327
20:05.470 --> 20:06.160
Yeah, hold on.

328
20:06.190 --> 20:07.900
Help me clean up.

329
20:09.010 --> 20:10.040
- Oh, wow. - Oh.

330
20:11.750 --> 20:13.120
Last time you ditched me,

331
20:13.570 --> 20:15.010
and I had to clean up all by myself.

332
20:15.850 --> 20:16.990
Now it’s your turn.

333
20:17.020 --> 20:19.120
See you next semester, Gun Gun, my best friend.

334
20:19.980 --> 20:21.180
Let’s go, Tyler.

335
20:21.220 --> 20:23.000
- See you, man. - See you.

336
20:23.040 --> 20:24.450
How can you do this to me?

337
20:25.110 --> 20:26.930
- Hey, you finish this. I’m done. - Hey.

338
20:29.960 --> 20:32.160
Wow!

339
20:32.180 --> 20:33.520
If you don’t mind…

340
20:33.570 --> 20:34.880
I want some meat.

341
20:36.130 --> 20:37.910
Hot, hot, hot.

342
20:38.360 --> 20:39.360
Careful.

343
20:39.440 --> 20:42.260
Crab stick, Ty’s favorite.

344
20:42.300 --> 20:43.100
Thank you.

345
20:43.130 --> 20:45.100
- And Kong’s favorite. - Thank you.

346
20:46.130 --> 20:48.130
I’ll go get more.

347
20:49.440 --> 20:51.800
There, there, Ji.

348
20:51.830 --> 20:52.830
Here.

349
20:53.330 --> 20:54.330
Thank you.

350
20:55.910 --> 20:56.910
But I didn’t ask.

351
20:57.900 --> 20:59.120
If you don’t want it…

352
20:59.340 --> 21:00.700
- Umm, take it. - Let me have some.

353
21:00.840 --> 21:02.540
Umm, take it. Hey, that’s my crab stick.

354
21:02.570 --> 21:03.756
- I know what it is. - My favorite.

355
21:03.780 --> 21:06.700
Hey, I thought Ruth was coming, too.

356
21:06.810 --> 21:07.970
Why isn’t he here?

357
21:08.190 --> 21:10.180
Ruth has a meeting at school.

358
21:10.220 --> 21:11.100
He’ll be here soon.

359
21:11.140 --> 21:13.520
Oh, he’s the class president, right?

360
21:14.600 --> 21:16.380
Unlike you, he has work to do.

361
21:16.410 --> 21:17.920
Zip it.

362
21:19.180 --> 21:21.070
Hey, Ji. Ruth’s here. Ruth’s here.

363
21:22.320 --> 21:23.660
I think that’s my dad.

364
21:23.900 --> 21:25.360
Maybe Ruth’s not coming.

365
21:25.580 --> 21:26.580
Are you two really close?

366
21:27.610 --> 21:29.250
Well… we’re pretty close.

367
21:30.670 --> 21:31.670
It’s true, Jean.

368
21:31.760 --> 21:33.980
Ji and Ruth are one step closer than the rest of us.

369
21:34.740 --> 21:38.590
Hmm, you guys have a way of measuring how close you are?

370
21:38.640 --> 21:39.500
Yeah.

371
21:39.550 --> 21:41.890
Ji doesn’t see Ruth as just a friend.

372
21:43.220 --> 21:43.930
- Ji... - Ahem!

373
21:43.960 --> 21:44.960
Tyler.

374
21:46.470 --> 21:48.020
I mean… Uh…

375
21:48.390 --> 21:50.500
Ji has known Ruth since they were kids.

376
21:50.530 --> 21:52.040
So they are really close.

377
21:52.080 --> 21:53.330
Yeah, close friends.

378
21:53.370 --> 21:54.910
- Right. - Right, Ji?

379
21:55.840 --> 21:57.220
Hey, Ruth’s here, Ji.

380
21:57.700 --> 21:58.700
Tyler.

381
22:01.680 --> 22:02.400
- Good evening. - Good evening.

382
22:02.440 --> 22:04.540
Oh, good evening, kids.

383
22:07.320 --> 22:08.320
Ji.

384
22:09.270 --> 22:10.740
When I was at the gate,

385
22:10.780 --> 22:13.110
I saw someone lurking around outside.

386
22:13.310 --> 22:14.840
I thought it was a burglar.

387
22:14.890 --> 22:16.616
But then I got a closer look and he resembled

388
22:16.640 --> 22:17.600
Diruth as a teenager.

389
22:17.630 --> 22:18.840
That’s when I figured it out.

390
22:19.300 --> 22:20.300
Oh, Ruth.

391
22:20.480 --> 22:21.576
- Good evening, ma’am. - Honey.

392
22:21.600 --> 22:23.200
I haven’t seen you for ages.

393
22:23.460 --> 22:24.760
You’re taller than Ji now.

394
22:25.000 --> 22:26.100
How are you doing?

395
22:26.370 --> 22:27.370
I’m great, ma’am.

396
22:27.660 --> 22:29.620
My mom and dad wanted me to give you this.

397
22:29.660 --> 22:30.660
Wow.

398
22:30.910 --> 22:32.750
How nice of Ms. Orn.

399
22:32.780 --> 22:34.970
- But I can’t... - Take it, honey.

400
22:35.020 --> 22:37.860
Diruth isn't someone who often spends money on us.

401
22:37.900 --> 22:40.360
I’ll make them some desserts sometime.

402
22:40.390 --> 22:41.986
- Thank you, ma’am. - Come on. Let’s eat.

403
22:42.010 --> 22:43.320
Go on. Let’s have dinner.

404
22:43.370 --> 22:44.280
Have a seat, son.

405
22:44.310 --> 22:45.310
- Here? - Have a seat.

406
22:52.340 --> 22:53.920
- Thank you. - This is delicious.

407
22:54.270 --> 22:56.510
- Can I have more crab sticks, please? - Can I have some?

408
22:57.560 --> 22:59.140
- You get one each. - Thank you.

409
23:04.440 --> 23:06.760
- Can I eat this now? - You’ll see.

410
23:06.790 --> 23:08.780
- Sorry, sorry. - Dad.

411
23:08.800 --> 23:10.060
I didn’t mean to.

412
23:12.460 --> 23:13.460
Thank you.

413
23:16.160 --> 23:17.520
There’s enough for everyone, kids.

414
23:34.140 --> 23:35.200
What the hell?

415
23:37.440 --> 23:39.440
I let Mhee attack me so many times

416
23:39.940 --> 23:40.980
before he let me hold him.

417
23:42.760 --> 23:44.040
I already told you, Ji,

418
23:44.540 --> 23:46.250
that Ruth is the most dangerous one.

419
23:47.360 --> 23:48.300
He brought gifts for your family.

420
23:48.330 --> 23:49.510
So when you visit his house,

421
23:49.540 --> 23:50.716
you should do the same, right?

422
23:50.740 --> 23:51.740
I think so.

423
23:52.580 --> 23:53.580
Now hold on.

424
23:53.860 --> 23:55.390
Why do I have to go to Ruth’s house?

425
23:55.430 --> 23:57.670
- You’ll have to go there eventually, right? - Umm, yeah.

426
24:10.300 --> 24:11.340
Did I say something wrong?

427
24:11.460 --> 24:12.460
You didn’t.

428
24:13.070 --> 24:14.070
Let’s eat.

429
24:15.060 --> 24:16.320
It’s just us now.

430
24:21.440 --> 24:22.840
You must have done something right.

431
24:22.970 --> 24:24.690
You got Mhee to sit on your lap.

432
24:25.280 --> 24:25.880
Really?

433
24:26.220 --> 24:27.220
Yeah.

434
24:29.640 --> 24:31.240
Did I do well?

435
24:35.290 --> 24:36.660
I never thought someone like you

436
24:36.690 --> 24:37.890
would care what I think.

437
24:40.200 --> 24:43.260
It didn’t take long for you to become my parents’ favorite.

438
24:44.050 --> 24:45.850
Since they found out we’d become close again,

439
24:46.120 --> 24:47.456
they couldn’t stop asking me about you.

440
24:47.480 --> 24:49.000
There’s no way they wouldn’t like you.

441
24:50.160 --> 24:51.200
But back then...

442
24:53.870 --> 24:55.176
If I hadn't let go of your hand...

443
24:55.200 --> 24:57.600
Would you have held my hand and followed me,

444
24:57.640 --> 24:59.116
leaving your own mother standing there,

445
24:59.140 --> 25:00.310
crying out for her son?

446
25:00.600 --> 25:02.640
I'd have been really mad at you if you'd done that.

447
25:05.810 --> 25:09.490
Besides... maybe I only befriended you back then

448
25:10.040 --> 25:11.996
because I was jealous of how rich your family was.

449
25:12.020 --> 25:13.050
Who knows?

450
25:23.790 --> 25:24.910
Are you free tomorrow?

451
25:26.820 --> 25:27.820
I think so.

452
25:28.020 --> 25:30.120
I guess I’ll just be lying around in bed.

453
25:30.450 --> 25:31.460
Then…

454
25:32.510 --> 25:33.630
Will you go out with me?

455
25:34.620 --> 25:36.680
Sure. Where and when?

456
25:36.910 --> 25:38.030
I’ll invite the others, too.

457
25:39.780 --> 25:40.980
Uh...

458
25:41.010 --> 25:42.140
You’ve invited them?

459
25:44.460 --> 25:45.460
I haven’t.

460
25:46.960 --> 25:47.960
Just you.

461
25:52.800 --> 25:54.310
I just want to go with you.

462
25:58.450 --> 26:00.380
Okay, just us two.

463
26:06.320 --> 26:10.580
- Meow, meow, meow, meow. - Meow, meow, meow, meow.

464
26:10.640 --> 26:11.900
Meow.

465
26:11.940 --> 26:13.550
Mhee, come out, Mhee.

466
26:13.570 --> 26:14.400
Mhee. Mhee.

467
26:14.440 --> 26:16.400
- Mhee, meow, meow. - Meow, meow, meow.

468
26:16.980 --> 26:19.740
- Meow, meow. - Meow, meow.

469
26:19.780 --> 26:21.270
Hey, you scared him.

470
26:21.300 --> 26:22.560
- Honey. - Hmm?

471
26:22.970 --> 26:25.070
- Are Ji’s friends all there? - Meow.

472
26:25.100 --> 26:27.510
- Meow. - Meow.

473
26:35.940 --> 26:36.940
You’re hungry?

474
26:37.580 --> 26:39.050
No, I’ve eaten at home.

475
26:40.290 --> 26:42.740
Let’s walk around until you get hungry then.

476
26:48.280 --> 26:49.280
You wanna go in there?

477
26:50.740 --> 26:51.740
Nah.

478
26:53.360 --> 26:54.360
Let’s do it.

479
27:03.240 --> 27:04.610
We don’t have to.

480
27:06.650 --> 27:07.650
Just do it.

481
27:08.270 --> 27:09.910
We might not get another chance tomorrow.

482
27:10.250 --> 27:11.080
Why would you say that?

483
27:11.110 --> 27:12.110
Who knows?

484
27:12.440 --> 27:13.740
It might come back someday.

485
27:14.300 --> 27:15.740
Just like vintage items.

486
27:16.430 --> 27:17.880
They always come back around.

487
27:19.740 --> 27:22.140
The only thing that makes a comeback is sticker photo booths,

488
27:22.570 --> 27:23.570
not us.

489
27:34.800 --> 27:35.800
Come closer.

490
27:39.140 --> 27:40.660
Your head is almost out of the frame.

491
27:41.440 --> 27:42.440
Move in.

492
27:44.300 --> 27:45.300
Ready?

493
28:15.650 --> 28:16.650
- Let me see. - Hey!

494
28:16.880 --> 28:17.550
No!

495
28:17.580 --> 28:18.760
The picture is blurry.

496
28:19.820 --> 28:21.020
Want to take another one?

497
28:21.050 --> 28:22.050
Hey, no!

498
28:25.250 --> 28:26.330
Wanna get something to eat?

499
28:26.590 --> 28:27.590
Sure.

500
28:28.540 --> 28:29.540
What do you wanna eat?

501
28:30.370 --> 28:31.560
Uh...

502
28:32.160 --> 28:33.160
Anything.

503
28:33.473 --> 28:35.340
How about noodles?

504
28:36.060 --> 28:37.246
No, I don’t want that.

505
28:38.020 --> 28:39.953
But you always have noodles at school.

506
28:39.973 --> 28:42.220
The food stalls at school mostly sell spicy food,

507
28:43.073 --> 28:44.260
fried food, and greasy food.

508
28:44.293 --> 28:45.906
How about Japanese food, then?

509
28:46.173 --> 28:47.922
Eating too much raw food might upset your stomach.

510
28:47.946 --> 28:49.420
How about sukiyaki or shabu?

511
28:49.453 --> 28:50.809
Didn't you just have that yesterday?

512
28:50.833 --> 28:51.660
How about the food court upstairs?

513
28:51.706 --> 28:53.906
That's no different from eating at the school cafeteria.

514
28:54.950 --> 28:55.950
Then…

515
28:56.760 --> 28:58.573
What do you wanna eat?

516
29:01.240 --> 29:01.893
Anything.

517
29:01.926 --> 29:02.926
Damn.

518
29:04.410 --> 29:06.726
Okay, okay. Whatever you want.

519
29:07.110 --> 29:09.640
Sorry, I don’t usually get to choose what to eat.

520
29:10.086 --> 29:11.086
Ruth!

521
29:11.920 --> 29:13.533
I knew it was you.

522
29:15.280 --> 29:17.053
Is this Ji?

523
29:18.340 --> 29:19.340
Nice to see you.

524
29:19.433 --> 29:20.000
Hello.

525
29:20.340 --> 29:21.746
I liked your gel candle.

526
29:22.880 --> 29:23.880
Thank you.

527
29:24.706 --> 29:25.706
What are you doing here?

528
29:25.773 --> 29:27.953
I told you I was coming to buy a camera today.

529
29:28.220 --> 29:30.273
Let's go eat. Mom's already inside.

530
29:37.010 --> 29:39.933
Ji, why don't you join us?

531
29:39.966 --> 29:41.293
The more, the merrier.

532
29:41.480 --> 29:43.426
I want to talk to you about Jean, too.

533
29:44.540 --> 29:45.980
- Okay. - Yay, let’s go.

534
29:53.260 --> 29:55.260
Ji, try this duck.

535
29:55.640 --> 29:57.506
The chef here is really good.

536
29:57.980 --> 29:59.100
Ruth, serve him some.

537
29:59.860 --> 30:01.380
Go ahead. Give him a generous portion.

538
30:01.453 --> 30:02.453
It's really delicious.

539
30:07.950 --> 30:09.286
The food here is so salty.

540
30:10.400 --> 30:11.640
Eat it while it's still hot.

541
30:22.920 --> 30:24.300
How is it? Good, right?

542
30:25.770 --> 30:27.786
Mm, it's delicious. Really delicious.

543
30:27.820 --> 30:28.460
Eat up, then.

544
30:28.500 --> 30:29.860
- Serve him more. - Okay.

545
30:29.900 --> 30:30.726
It’s just so good.

546
30:30.760 --> 30:31.646
I’m good.

547
30:31.666 --> 30:32.946
- Let’s eat together. - Don’t be shy.

548
30:32.970 --> 30:35.500
It’s my treat.

549
30:35.533 --> 30:36.902
- Eat up, you two. - Have some duck skin.

550
30:36.926 --> 30:38.040
I’ll just eat tomatoes.

551
30:38.080 --> 30:39.786
- Don’t be shy. - It’s okay. Eat up.

552
30:40.810 --> 30:42.066
1…2…3.

553
30:44.300 --> 30:46.300
Smile, 1…2…3.

554
30:49.540 --> 30:50.706
One more. One more.

555
30:52.600 --> 30:53.920
- 1…2…3. - He’s just like his dad.

556
30:55.560 --> 30:56.560
Sorry?

557
30:59.700 --> 31:00.700
Ruth.

558
31:01.380 --> 31:03.153
Of all my three children,

559
31:03.910 --> 31:05.900
Ruth takes after his father the most.

560
31:07.160 --> 31:07.966
1…2…3.

561
31:08.006 --> 31:09.253
Though he seems quiet,

562
31:09.613 --> 31:10.813
he’s very picky.

563
31:11.510 --> 31:12.740
Especially with his food.

564
31:18.440 --> 31:19.666
Thank you so much, Ji.

565
31:21.360 --> 31:23.533
Me? About what, ma’am?

566
31:26.560 --> 31:28.120
Since the new semester started,

567
31:28.606 --> 31:30.706
Ruth seems so much more lively.

568
31:31.300 --> 31:32.300
That's thanks to you.

569
31:34.450 --> 31:37.906
I know about Ji, the good boy,

570
31:40.120 --> 31:42.240
and that... what was it?

571
31:42.266 --> 31:44.666
You guys splashing water at each other in the boys' bathroom.

572
31:45.060 --> 31:46.386
Lita told me about it.

573
31:47.760 --> 31:48.922
I think that was the first time

574
31:48.946 --> 31:50.920
Ruth had ever been scolded by a teacher.

575
31:55.680 --> 31:56.680
Here.

576
31:57.080 --> 31:58.080
That means you like it?

577
31:59.620 --> 32:01.460
Though we've always lived under the same roof,

578
32:02.660 --> 32:04.433
it feels like I've got my son back.

579
32:07.793 --> 32:08.820
One more.

580
32:09.233 --> 32:10.233
Okay.

581
32:28.106 --> 32:30.100
Yo, Ji, my brother!

582
32:31.680 --> 32:32.680
Hello.

583
32:34.510 --> 32:36.646
Why are you here so early, Ji?

584
32:37.126 --> 32:38.713
How did I get here after someone who's

585
32:38.733 --> 32:40.093
been late for five years straight?

586
32:44.040 --> 32:45.367
Do I look bad?

587
32:45.629 --> 32:47.680
No, it suits you.

588
32:48.010 --> 32:49.498
- Beautiful. - So cute.

589
32:52.420 --> 32:53.229
- Stop! - Ouch!

590
32:53.250 --> 32:54.378
Stop it.

591
32:54.843 --> 32:57.309
You do have a way with words, just like Pim said.

592
32:57.352 --> 32:59.760
Doesn’t your hair get in the way when you play basketball?

593
32:59.803 --> 33:02.181
No. I’m coaching this year.

594
33:02.669 --> 33:05.650
And after that, I’ll quit the basketball club.

595
33:09.000 --> 33:11.156
Seeing everyone else doing what they want,

596
33:11.480 --> 33:13.883
I don't know why I should keep forcing myself to do this.

597
33:15.010 --> 33:16.247
Great job, Ked.

598
33:16.632 --> 33:19.410
After you quit, let’s go have egg yolk ice-cream.

599
33:19.738 --> 33:23.207
Is that all you think about, Ty?

600
33:24.520 --> 33:26.240
Come on. Let’s get to work.

601
33:27.020 --> 33:28.974
Please come in.

602
33:33.490 --> 33:35.098
Where are the school council members?

603
33:35.490 --> 33:37.161
I heard they had a meeting in the morning.

604
33:37.185 --> 33:38.185
They’ll be here after.

605
33:38.710 --> 33:39.890
What have you done?

606
33:40.101 --> 33:41.890
I said, blue. Blue.

607
33:42.087 --> 33:43.432
This is blue. See?

608
33:43.461 --> 33:45.134
That’s not blue. That’s green.

609
33:45.200 --> 33:47.403
The bucket is purple, but the paint is blue.

610
33:47.447 --> 33:48.138
Are you blind?

611
33:48.160 --> 33:49.032
- It’s green. - See?

612
33:49.076 --> 33:50.303
- It’s not green. - Here. This is blue.

613
33:50.327 --> 33:51.614
That is dark blue.

614
33:51.840 --> 33:52.632
- That’s not blue. - It is.

615
33:52.661 --> 33:54.305
- It’s blue. See? - It’s green.

616
33:54.356 --> 33:55.774
Wrong. You’re wrong.

617
33:55.796 --> 33:56.356
Gun,

618
33:56.632 --> 33:58.050
don’t you have a sport practice?

619
33:58.087 --> 33:59.221
What are you doing here?

620
33:59.818 --> 34:01.220
Why can’t I be here?

621
34:01.374 --> 34:02.374
I want to be here.

622
34:03.083 --> 34:04.007
Here’s a thing.

623
34:04.008 --> 34:06.800
- Gun was in art club, right? - Go on.

624
34:06.850 --> 34:10.545
And actually, I didn't design this colored backdrop all by myself.

625
34:10.756 --> 34:12.058
Gun helped, too?

626
34:12.618 --> 34:14.203
Huh? Gun helped you?

627
34:14.429 --> 34:16.174
- Yes. Gun designed this. - This one?

628
34:16.225 --> 34:17.225
Mmm.

629
34:18.180 --> 34:21.236
I can’t believe someone like Gun

630
34:22.720 --> 34:24.901
can be useful, too.

631
34:24.938 --> 34:26.647
Watch your mouth, Ler.

632
34:26.683 --> 34:28.930
Stop fighting and get this done.

633
34:28.967 --> 34:29.840
So we can go home.

634
34:29.970 --> 34:32.429
I’m sorry but I’m already home.

635
34:32.458 --> 34:33.458
Shut up.

636
34:35.510 --> 34:36.510
Guys!

637
34:37.900 --> 34:39.403
Water Dragon Attack!

638
34:39.432 --> 34:39.941
- Hey! - Hey!

639
34:40.000 --> 34:41.416
- It’s spilling on me. - You’re gonna mess this up, Tyler.

640
34:41.440 --> 34:42.836
You’re ruining the work.

641
34:43.090 --> 34:44.203
Hey! Oh, no.

642
34:47.890 --> 34:49.076
Damn it, Ler!

643
34:49.112 --> 34:50.443
I’m sorry, bro!

644
34:50.487 --> 34:52.414
I’m sorry. Help me!

645
34:52.450 --> 34:53.621
Ji, help me!

646
34:55.643 --> 34:56.829
Ji, help me, Ji.

647
34:56.850 --> 34:59.643
- Please, no, no, no. - Take this.

648
35:01.720 --> 35:02.887
There you go.

649
35:12.340 --> 35:14.290
Take this. Take this.

650
35:18.940 --> 35:21.905
Guys, here comes the food.

651
35:22.225 --> 35:23.709
Come and eat.

652
35:23.745 --> 35:25.716
Come on. Here are the chopsticks and plates.

653
35:25.745 --> 35:27.621
Hey, I’m hungry. Let me have some.

654
35:28.070 --> 35:29.070
Hey, come on, come on.

655
35:29.280 --> 35:30.596
Come on now.

656
35:36.100 --> 35:37.280
- Wow. - Wow.

657
35:37.316 --> 35:37.905
Oh my gosh.

658
35:37.941 --> 35:38.941
You’re not eating?

659
35:39.076 --> 35:40.680
No, I’m not hungry.

660
35:42.420 --> 35:43.876
You’re late, Mr. President.

661
35:46.050 --> 35:47.127
I had to finish something.

662
35:47.730 --> 35:48.807
About the Sports Day?

663
35:50.940 --> 35:52.116
It’s not that.

664
35:55.890 --> 35:58.170
The teacher entered me in the science project competition.

665
35:58.580 --> 36:00.414
My name has already been submitted,

666
36:00.887 --> 36:01.887
so I can’t withdraw.

667
36:03.300 --> 36:04.380
Will it take the whole day?

668
36:04.516 --> 36:05.890
My competition is in the morning.

669
36:07.390 --> 36:09.150
By the time everyone else finishes competing

670
36:10.480 --> 36:11.745
and I get back to school,

671
36:12.116 --> 36:13.436
Sports Day will probably be over.

672
36:15.330 --> 36:16.407
It’s okay.

673
36:16.989 --> 36:18.400
It’s just Sports Day.

674
36:18.669 --> 36:20.610
You still have the Open House to work on.

675
36:21.112 --> 36:22.116
Don’t worry too much.

676
36:27.810 --> 36:28.996
There’s paint on your face.

677
36:29.540 --> 36:30.058
Really?

678
36:30.385 --> 36:32.050
- Where is the paint… - Hey.

679
36:32.580 --> 36:33.580
Don’t touch.

680
36:33.796 --> 36:34.876
You’re gonna make it worse.

681
36:42.189 --> 36:43.189
Uh...

682
36:43.540 --> 36:46.007
Why are your hands so sticky?

683
36:47.460 --> 36:48.698
Don't tell me...

684
36:48.734 --> 36:50.734
The hand you're using to wipe me with

685
36:50.763 --> 36:53.047
is the same hand you used to hold that paintbrush.

686
36:58.770 --> 37:00.763
I'm not getting messy all by myself!

687
37:00.800 --> 37:01.978
No, no, no.

688
37:02.378 --> 37:03.378
Come here.

689
37:03.832 --> 37:04.832
No, no, no, no.

690
37:05.425 --> 37:06.210
Hey, what’s that?

691
37:06.385 --> 37:07.018
What?

692
37:07.323 --> 37:08.625
I’m not gonna fall for that.

693
37:08.800 --> 37:09.898
Stop, stop, stop!

694
37:10.465 --> 37:11.465
- Stop, stop! - No.

695
37:12.740 --> 37:13.694
- Yes. - No, no, no,

696
37:13.723 --> 37:15.432
- Yes. - No, no, no, no, no, no.

697
37:16.490 --> 37:17.243
- See you. - See you.

698
37:17.287 --> 37:18.567
Thank you. Thanks a lot.

699
37:18.589 --> 37:19.876
- Bye-bye. - Bye-bye.

700
37:20.072 --> 37:21.658
- See you later. - See you. Bye.

701
37:21.687 --> 37:22.687
Bye-bye.

702
37:31.200 --> 37:32.960
Ruth, your car’s here.

703
37:33.352 --> 37:34.130
Bye-bye.

704
37:34.160 --> 37:35.570
See you tomorrow.

705
37:35.985 --> 37:36.985
Mmm.

706
37:37.345 --> 37:38.345
See you.

707
37:51.530 --> 37:53.229
Wow, Ji, look at that.

708
37:54.320 --> 37:55.320
Look at what?

709
37:55.861 --> 37:57.701
It's just like the drama I watched last night.

710
37:58.600 --> 38:00.545
The girl marries into the guy's family,

711
38:00.567 --> 38:02.043
but his parents don’t like her.

712
38:02.625 --> 38:03.625
Exactly.

713
38:03.825 --> 38:04.825
Tyler!

714
38:05.090 --> 38:06.090
Look at his face.

715
38:06.850 --> 38:08.560
I’ll go home, then.

716
38:08.596 --> 38:09.869
- See you tomorrow. - See you.

717
38:10.480 --> 38:11.047
Bye-bye.

718
38:11.440 --> 38:12.440
See you later.

719
38:18.540 --> 38:19.818
Was that boy Jira’s son?

720
38:25.540 --> 38:26.540
Yes.

721
38:30.870 --> 38:33.270
Are you withdrawing from the competition because of that boy?

722
38:54.800 --> 38:55.876
(Morning, Ji.)

723
38:55.927 --> 38:57.360
Did that hurt?

724
38:57.556 --> 38:59.832
You said you wanted to show me something.

725
39:02.740 --> 39:04.865
Ta da!

726
39:08.650 --> 39:10.341
Why aren’t you excited?

727
39:11.230 --> 39:12.230
Oh!

728
39:12.320 --> 39:13.320
Wow!

729
39:14.350 --> 39:16.065
That phone is so cool!

730
39:16.283 --> 39:17.883
Look. It can do this.

731
39:18.261 --> 39:19.563
With this bad boy,

732
39:19.614 --> 39:21.560
we can FaceTime each other whenever we want.

733
39:22.740 --> 39:24.786
But we’re already seeing each other’s face all day long.

734
39:24.810 --> 39:26.589
Because you don’t have this,

735
39:27.010 --> 39:28.570
your relationship’s not going anywhere.

736
39:29.350 --> 39:30.916
Thanks for your advice.

737
39:31.265 --> 39:32.265
But I didn’t need it.

738
39:34.880 --> 39:36.130
Hey, how do you have this?

739
39:36.741 --> 39:38.960
It’s brand new. I just got it.

740
39:39.003 --> 39:40.509
Does it have eFootball?

741
39:40.530 --> 39:41.576
There’s only this. Jump, jump.

742
39:41.600 --> 39:42.909
You have to get in line, Gun.

743
39:43.047 --> 39:45.425
No, no, no, no. Hey, hey, hey.

744
39:45.469 --> 39:46.676
Hula Hula Hooray

745
39:46.712 --> 39:48.000
Hooray Hooray Hula

746
39:48.036 --> 39:50.472
Go, Red, Go

747
39:50.509 --> 39:51.534
Hooray Hooray Hula

748
39:51.563 --> 39:52.625
Hooray Hooray Hula

749
39:52.654 --> 39:53.869
Go, Red, Go

750
40:10.000 --> 40:11.512
I’m Kwan from Class 2.

751
40:12.670 --> 40:14.130
I’m Ji from Class 7.

752
40:14.174 --> 40:15.054
I know.

753
40:15.098 --> 40:16.770
Your name is on your shirt.

754
40:19.287 --> 40:20.287
Ji.

755
40:20.710 --> 40:21.170
Hey,

756
40:21.192 --> 40:22.232
What are you doing here?

757
40:22.269 --> 40:23.403
I was just walking around.

758
40:23.796 --> 40:25.338
I should ask you. What are you doing here?

759
40:25.352 --> 40:28.261
The student council hasn't had much work lately.

760
40:28.305 --> 40:29.963
Mmm. By the way…

761
40:33.450 --> 40:34.836
Kwan is back to playing ping pong.

762
40:37.781 --> 40:39.780
You know Kwan?

763
40:40.170 --> 40:41.170
Yeah.

764
40:43.025 --> 40:44.203
The drama club president.

765
40:45.890 --> 40:47.105
Oh.

766
40:49.530 --> 40:50.974
The stage play.

767
40:52.660 --> 40:53.660
Mmm.

768
40:54.880 --> 40:56.785
Where are you going after school?

769
40:57.410 --> 40:59.716
I’ll leave at 3 p.m.

770
41:00.247 --> 41:02.865
I have to take Tyler to rent some new manga near my house today.

771
41:07.141 --> 41:08.141
Wanna come with us?

772
41:10.327 --> 41:12.465
- Sure. - Let’s go.

773
41:20.610 --> 41:22.378
Hi, Ji, Ty.

774
41:22.407 --> 41:24.123
- Hello. - Has your school started?

775
41:24.552 --> 41:26.120
Yes. This is our first day.

776
41:26.152 --> 41:27.047
Ah.

777
41:27.069 --> 41:29.040
Have the new mangas arrived yet?

778
41:29.069 --> 41:30.138
Yeah, they’re here.

779
41:32.130 --> 41:32.749
Here.

780
41:33.090 --> 41:34.090
Thank you.

781
41:34.770 --> 41:35.896
There's an old horror manga I've been wanting

782
41:35.920 --> 41:37.643
to get my hands on, Chok.

783
41:37.687 --> 41:38.687
Do you have it?

784
41:43.760 --> 41:44.760
Hey.

785
41:45.280 --> 41:46.280
Is this the one?

786
41:46.690 --> 41:47.483
It’s not.

787
41:47.520 --> 41:50.160
This one came out two years before the volume Tyler is looking for.

788
41:53.230 --> 41:55.003
Hey, is it this one?

789
41:55.025 --> 41:56.036
Oh, yes.

790
42:26.640 --> 42:28.392
Ji, what happened? I’m here.

791
42:31.860 --> 42:32.860
Nothing.

792
42:33.061 --> 42:34.909
I’ve found the manga you’re looking for.

793
42:35.240 --> 42:37.883
Don’t come in here. There’s no space.

794
42:58.720 --> 43:00.552
Hey, Ji, what happened?

795
43:00.596 --> 43:01.881
Why did you just leave Ruth in there?

796
43:01.905 --> 43:03.840
Are you two fighting?

797
43:05.740 --> 43:08.516
Hey, why are your ears so red?

798
43:12.230 --> 43:14.603
It’s you who came into my life

799
43:14.640 --> 43:17.309
You light up my new beginning

800
43:17.352 --> 43:19.629
Once weary heart, you make it full

801
43:19.672 --> 43:22.036
Oh, don’t tell me you…

802
43:22.065 --> 43:25.192
Of hope with the love from you

803
43:25.214 --> 43:28.894
Turning my world into a dream come true

804
43:28.923 --> 43:30.530
It’s you who came into my life

805
43:30.567 --> 43:32.916
You light up my new beginning

806
43:33.498 --> 43:34.305
Stop it.

807
43:34.334 --> 43:37.440
Because of you, I want to keep going -You’ve got your manga. Now go home. Bye.

808
43:37.498 --> 43:41.978
Whatever fate may bring, whatever is in store

809
43:42.007 --> 43:45.716
In you, I find hope once more

810
44:16.430 --> 44:17.767
Once we cross that finish line,

811
44:18.730 --> 44:20.050
we won't be just friends anymore.

812
44:25.680 --> 44:27.490
I won the science project competition.

813
44:27.890 --> 44:28.890
Where's my reward?
